  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 192,
      "text": "MEXICO\n66. Additional measures would help the financial system remain resilient in a changing\nfinancial and regulatory landscape. While systemic vulnerabilities are found to be contained, the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 192,
      "end_char": 376,
      "text": "2022 FSAP flags the need for upgrading the financial sector oversight and crisis management\nframeworks to close some gaps and address emerging challenges. After aligning the legal and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 376,
      "end_char": 562,
      "text": "regulatory AML/CFT framework with Financial Action Task Force standards, the focus should now be\non strengthening the AML/CFT regime, including through adequate resourcing, ensuring the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 562,
      "end_char": 778,
      "text": "availability of high-quality beneficial ownership information, and monitoring emerging financial\nintegrity risks related to fintech.\n67. Unlocking growth potential and reducing inequality require a broad supply side\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 778,
      "end_char": 969,
      "text": "agenda. Despite increased trade openness and macroeconomic stability, productivity growth has\nbeen weak and the growth in output per worker has averaged close to zero over the past 15 years.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 969,
      "end_char": 1166,
      "text": "The authorities’ agenda addresses some obstacles to higher productivity and growth, but additional\nefforts are needed to address corruption, crime, and the weak rule of law; increase human capital\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1166,
      "end_char": 1355,
      "text": "investments and address infrastructure bottlenecks; and reduce labor and product market rigidities.\n68. Financial inclusion should be deepened to support inclusive growth. The potential of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1355,
      "end_char": 1546,
      "text": "digital finance to increase financial access and depth should be fostered through increased\ncompetition in the financial sector, while maintaining safeguard to ensure financial stability and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1546,
      "end_char": 1755,
      "text": "integrity. Efforts to broaden digital connectivity and to improve the transparency of financial services\nshould continue.\n69. Determined implementation of the anticorruption framework will be key to enhancing\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1755,
      "end_char": 1972,
      "text": "its effectiveness. Steps should include strengthening prevention, facilitating reporting including\nwhistleblower protection, and further empowering institutions in charge of investigation,\nprosecution, and oversight.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1972,
      "end_char": 2151,
      "text": "70. A gradual increase in productive government spending, financed by reforms to raise\ntax revenues, would promote growth and equity. Higher spending on education, health, public\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2151,
      "end_char": 2353,
      "text": "investment, and social protection is critical to improve human and physical capital and to narrow the\nsignificant variation in social outcomes across states. To be effective, this higher spending would\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2353,
      "end_char": 2536,
      "text": "need to be accompanied by more efficient public spending, building on recent steps taken to\nimprove spending control and program design. Recent tax administration reforms have buoyed\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2536,
      "end_char": 2725,
      "text": "revenue, but a well-designed tax policy reform is needed to reduce differences in VAT rates, reduce\ntax expenditures, and widen the top personal income tax bracket. These reforms should be\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2725,
      "end_char": 2890,
      "text": "combined with adequate compensation to offset the impact on poorer households.\n71. Recent labor market reforms should be adapted to lessen their negative effects on\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2890,
      "end_char": 3070,
      "text": "formal sector employment. The current strategy could be complemented by continued\nimplementation of the labor dispute resolution mechanisms; lowering firing restrictions; reducing\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3070,
      "end_char": 3252,
      "text": "the regulatory costs of formalizing a business; and aligning increases in the real minimum wage to\nincreases in the productivity of lower wage workers.\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 31"
    }
  ]
}

